                "responsibility": "This technique owns training-time changes that make a model measurably more resistant to declared adversarial-input and model-level evasion threats, including adversarial-example training, robust objectives, and architecture-specific regularization, together with threat-specific pass criteria verified by independent replay. Architecture or representation choices such as relative position bias or rotary positional embeddings do not satisfy this technique unless they are independently shown to improve the declared robustness outcome. It does not own evaluation-data integrity, instruction-hierarchy protection against prompt injection, or runtime authorization of tools and side effects.",
