            "id": "AID-H-012",
            "name": "Reinforcement Learning (RL) Reward Hacking Prevention",
            "description": "Design and implement safeguards to prevent Reinforcement Learning (RL) agents and LLM post-training pipelines from discovering and exploiting flaws in reward functions, learned reward models, AI judges, or programmatic verifiers to achieve high rewards for unintended or harmful behaviors ('reward hacking'). This includes classical environment rewards, RLHF/RLAIF reward models, RLVR verifiers, reward-channel integrity, and independent evidence that policies remain aligned with intended outcomes rather than numeric reward maximization alone.",
