                    "phase": [
                        "building"
                    ],
                    "description": "Design and maintain robust, unambiguous system prompts that clearly separate trusted instructions from untrusted content, state instruction precedence, and reduce the attack surface for prompt injection and jailbreak attempts. This technique focuses on structure (delimiters, namespaces), precedence (policy > system > developer > user), and safe inclusion of dynamic context. In current practitioner language, these patterns include spotlighting, datamarking, encoding, and other instruction/data separation techniques that mark untrusted content as data rather than authority.",
