                        {
                            "id": "AID-H-017.002-G001",
                            "implementation": "Design granular, single-purpose tools instead of overly-permissive ones.",
                            "howTo": "<h5>Concept:</h5><p>Do not expose a generic <code>execute_sql</code> capability. Publish narrow methods with typed parameters, explicit result projection, bounded cardinality, and a database identity that cannot write or read unrelated tables.</p><h5>Step 1: Implement narrow database tools</h5><pre><code class=\"language-python\"># File: agent_tools/customer_reads.py\nfrom __future__ import annotations\nimport os\n\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\n\nfrom psycopg import Connection\nfrom psycopg.rows import dict_row\n\ndef _required_positive_int(name: str) -&gt; int:\n    value = int(os.environ[name])\n    if value &lt;= 0:\n        raise RuntimeError(f\"{name} must be a positive integer\")\n    return value\n\nORDER_QUERY_DEFAULT_LIMIT = _required_positive_int(\"VERIFIED_H017_ORDER_QUERY_DEFAULT_LIMIT\")\nORDER_QUERY_MAX_LIMIT = _required_positive_int(\"VERIFIED_H017_ORDER_QUERY_MAX_LIMIT\")\n\n\n\nif ORDER_QUERY_DEFAULT_LIMIT &gt; ORDER_QUERY_MAX_LIMIT:\n    raise RuntimeError(\"verified default order limit exceeds maximum\")\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass CustomerReadTools:\n    connection: Connection\n\n    def get_user_by_id(self, user_id: int) -&gt; dict | None:\n        if isinstance(user_id, bool) or not isinstance(user_id, int) or user_id &lt;= 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"user_id must be a positive integer\")\n        with self.connection.cursor(row_factory=dict_row) as cursor:\n            cursor.execute(\n                \"SELECT user_id, status, plan FROM agent_safe.customer_directory WHERE user_id = %s\",\n                (user_id,),\n            )\n            return cursor.fetchone()\n\n    def get_user_orders(self, user_id: int, limit: int = ORDER_QUERY_DEFAULT_LIMIT) -&gt; list[dict]:\n        if isinstance(user_id, bool) or not isinstance(user_id, int) or user_id &lt;= 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"user_id must be a positive integer\")\n        if isinstance(limit, bool) or not isinstance(limit, int) or not 1 &lt;= limit &lt;= ORDER_QUERY_MAX_LIMIT:\n            raise ValueError(\"limit must be inside the verified order-query policy\")\n        with self.connection.cursor(row_factory=dict_row) as cursor:\n            cursor.execute(\n                \"SELECT order_id, created_at, state FROM agent_safe.order_summary WHERE user_id = %s ORDER BY created_at DESC LIMIT %s\",\n                (user_id, limit),\n            )\n            return list(cursor.fetchall())\n</code></pre><h5>Step 2: Enforce a read-only database role</h5><pre><code class=\"language-sql\">CREATE ROLE agent_customer_reader LOGIN;\nALTER ROLE agent_customer_reader SET default_transaction_read_only = on;\nGRANT USAGE ON SCHEMA agent_safe TO agent_customer_reader;\nGRANT SELECT ON agent_safe.customer_directory, agent_safe.order_summary TO agent_customer_reader;\nREVOKE CREATE ON SCHEMA public FROM agent_customer_reader;\n</code></pre><p><strong>Privilege boundary:</strong> <code>default_transaction_read_only</code> is defense in depth and is session-overridable; the real write barrier is ownership plus explicit table/schema privileges, which must be read back and tested independently. Do not grant this role ownership, <code>SUPERUSER</code>, <code>BYPASSRLS</code>, or any write privilege.</p><p><strong>Verification evidence:</strong> Export the published tool schema, database grants, and a negative test showing the role cannot insert, update, delete, access non-approved tables, or submit arbitrary SQL. Re-run the permission readback on every role or schema change and fail the release if a generic query parameter or write privilege appears.</p><p><strong>Action:</strong> Register only the two typed methods above with the agent runtime; keep the connection and SQL text server-owned.</p><h5>Keep the action safely bounded</h5><p>Reconcile the complete population of every registered tool operation, route, query, and permission in the agent's assigned tool set; reject expired, revoked, or stale policy and asset bindings under the policy-defined freshness window.</p>"
                        }
