                    "implementationGuidance": [
                        {
                            "id": "AID-H-018.001-G001",
                            "implementation": "Use Pydantic or JSON Schema to enforce tool parameter schemas at dispatch time.",
                            "howTo": "<h5>Concept:</h5><p>Tool parameter validation belongs in the dispatcher, not inside individual tools. The dispatcher should reject unknown tools, reject non-object payloads, validate against strict schemas, and only invoke the tool with the validated result.</p><h5>Step 1: Define strict schemas for each tool</h5><pre><code class=\"language-python\"># File: agent/tool_schemas.py\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport os\nfrom typing import Literal\n\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel, ConfigDict, Field, ValidationError, constr\n\nSUBJECT_MIN_LENGTH = int(os.environ[\"VERIFIED_H018_EMAIL_SUBJECT_MIN_CHARACTERS\"])\nSUBJECT_MAX_LENGTH = int(os.environ[\"VERIFIED_H018_EMAIL_SUBJECT_MAX_CHARACTERS\"])\nif SUBJECT_MIN_LENGTH < 1 or SUBJECT_MAX_LENGTH < SUBJECT_MIN_LENGTH:\n    raise RuntimeError(\"verified email-subject bounds are invalid\")\n\n\nclass GetStockPriceParams(BaseModel):\n    model_config = ConfigDict(extra=\"forbid\", strict=True, str_strip_whitespace=True)\n    ticker: constr(pattern=r\"^[A-Z]{1,5}$\")\n\n\nclass SendEmailParams(BaseModel):\n    model_config = ConfigDict(extra=\"forbid\", strict=True, str_strip_whitespace=True)\n    recipient: constr(pattern=r\"^[^@\\s]+@[^@\\s]+\\.[^@\\s]+$\")\n    subject: constr(min_length=SUBJECT_MIN_LENGTH, max_length=SUBJECT_MAX_LENGTH)\n    priority: Literal[\"high\", \"normal\", \"low\"] = \"normal\"\n</code></pre><h5>Step 2: Fail closed in the dispatcher</h5><pre><code class=\"language-python\"># File: agent/dispatcher.py\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom collections.abc import Callable\nimport json\nimport logging\nfrom typing import Any\n\nfrom pydantic import ValidationError\n\nfrom .handlers import get_stock_price, send_email\nfrom .tool_schemas import GetStockPriceParams, SendEmailParams\n\n\nclass ToolDispatchRejected(Exception):\n    pass\n\n\nToolHandler = Callable[..., Any]\nlogger = logging.getLogger(\"agent.tool_dispatch\")\n\nTOOL_SCHEMAS = {\n    \"get_stock_price\": GetStockPriceParams,\n    \"send_email\": SendEmailParams,\n}\nTOOL_HANDLERS: dict[str, ToolHandler] = {\n    \"get_stock_price\": get_stock_price,\n    \"send_email\": send_email,\n}\n\n\ndef log_security_event(event: str, **fields: Any) -&gt; None:\n    logger.info(json.dumps({\"event\": event, **fields}, sort_keys=True, default=str))\n\n\n\ndef dispatch_tool(tool_name: str, raw_params: dict, request_id: str) -&gt; Any:\n    if not isinstance(request_id, str) or not request_id:\n        raise ToolDispatchRejected(\"request_id is required\")\n    schema = TOOL_SCHEMAS.get(tool_name)\n    handler = TOOL_HANDLERS.get(tool_name)\n    if schema is None or handler is None:\n        log_security_event(\"tool_param_validation_failed\", request_id=request_id, tool_name=tool_name, reason=\"unknown_tool\")\n        raise ToolDispatchRejected(f\"unknown tool: {tool_name}\")\n    if not isinstance(raw_params, dict):\n        log_security_event(\"tool_param_validation_failed\", request_id=request_id, tool_name=tool_name, reason=\"arguments_not_object\")\n        raise ToolDispatchRejected(\"tool arguments must be a JSON object\")\n\n    try:\n        validated = schema.model_validate(raw_params)\n    except ValidationError as exc:\n        log_security_event(\n            \"tool_param_validation_failed\",\n            request_id=request_id,\n            tool_name=tool_name,\n            errors=exc.errors(),\n        )\n        raise ToolDispatchRejected(f\"invalid parameters for {tool_name}\") from exc\n\n    log_security_event(\n        \"tool_param_validation_passed\",\n        request_id=request_id,\n        tool_name=tool_name,\n        schema_name=schema.__name__,\n    )\n    return handler(**validated.model_dump())\n</code></pre><h5>Step 3: Return a structured deny result to the agent loop</h5><pre><code class=\"language-python\"># File: agent/tool_runtime.py\nfrom .dispatcher import ToolDispatchRejected, dispatch_tool\n\n\ndef handle_tool_call(tool_name: str, raw_params: dict, request_id: str) -&gt; dict:\n    try:\n        result = dispatch_tool(tool_name, raw_params, request_id)\n        return {\"status\": \"ok\", \"result\": result}\n    except ToolDispatchRejected as exc:\n        return {\"status\": \"blocked\", \"reason\": str(exc)}\n</code></pre><p><strong>Verification evidence:</strong> Unit-test unknown tools, non-object arguments, extra keys, malformed values, and handler non-invocation on every deny path. Retain structured allow/deny events with tool name, schema version, dispatcher release, and request correlation ID in the external audit pipeline; independently replay the negative corpus before promotion.</p><p><strong>Action:</strong> Validate every LLM-produced tool call at dispatch time, forbid unknown keys with <code>extra=&quot;forbid&quot;</code>, and never pass raw model output directly into a tool implementation.</p><h5>Keep the action safely bounded</h5><p>Reconcile the complete population of every registered tool call and raw parameter object presented to the dispatcher; reject expired, revoked, or stale policy and asset bindings under the policy-defined freshness window.</p>"
                        }
                    ],
