                  "comparison": "AID-H-022 owns change risk and hostile installation behavior; AID-H-023 owns publisher identity, registry workflow, trusted CI release origin, and package provenance.\nA trusted publisher can ship a risky change, and a safe-looking change can come from a compromised publisher path."
