            "description": "A critical supply chain defense that ensures software packages (e.g., NPM, PyPI) are published only from a secure, auditable, and authorized source. This technique reduces credential-only publishing attacks where a stolen developer credential is used to publish a malicious version of a legitimate package. It achieves this by prohibiting publications from local developer machines and mandating that all releases originate from a hardened CI/CD pipeline that authenticates using short-lived, identity-based tokens and generates verifiable provenance attestations.",
