              "implementationGuidance": [
                {
                  "id": "AID-H-033.004-G001",
                  "implementation": "Store route policy bundles in version control, require approval for changes, canary high-risk routing changes, and support immediate rollback.",
                  "howTo": "<h5>Concept:</h5><p>Route bundles are security artifacts. They should be versioned, signed, reviewed, canaried, and rolled back exactly like firewall or admission policy, not treated as ad-hoc application config.</p><h5>Step 1: Version the route bundle and publish a signed manifest</h5><pre><code class=\"language-json\">{\n  \"bundle_version\": \"2026.04.12-1\",\n  \"policy_path\": \"routing/bundles/2026.04.12-1.rego\",\n  \"approvers\": [\"platform-security\", \"ai-governance\"],\n  \"rollout_mode\": \"canary\"\n}\n</code></pre><h5>Step 2: Canary the bundle before full promotion</h5><pre><code class=\"language-python\"># File: routing/canary_bundle.py\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\n\nmanifest = json.loads(Path(\"routing/route_bundle_manifest.json\").read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\nprint({\"bundle_version\": manifest[\"bundle_version\"], \"rollout_mode\": manifest[\"rollout_mode\"], \"status\": \"canary_started\"})\n</code></pre><h5>Step 3: Roll back on safety or mismatch spikes</h5><p>Track route-decision mismatches, moderation regressions, or policy evaluation failures against the active bundle version. If those signals spike during canary, immediately restore the prior approved bundle version.</p><p><strong>Action:</strong> Keep route bundles in version control with explicit approval and rollback records. High-risk routing changes should never jump directly to full production rollout.</p><h5>Keep the action safely bounded</h5><p>At the CI release gate, canary router, and runtime bundle loader before a route revision becomes authoritative, bind a signed, versioned policy (policy version and SHA-256 digest) to the exact asset_id and asset version for route bundle, schema, source revision, signer and trust root, test suite, canary cohort, rollback target, gateway release, and runtime instance inventory. Reconcile the complete population of every bundle change, required policy test, canary decision, runtime instance, and rollback/readback target; reject expired, revoked, or stale policy and asset bindings under the policy-defined freshness window.</p><h5>Verify safely</h5><p>A separately credentialed verifier independently replays source-to-bundle provenance, tests, canary metrics/decisions, activation and rollback with tamper, missing approval, stale signer, mixed fleet, bad canary, loader outage, and rollback fixtures, reads back effective state from the enforcement system, exercises positive, negative, boundary, stale-evidence, and dependency-failure fixtures, and reconciles every eligible item.</p>"
                }
              ]
