                    "description": "This control owns only effective route identity resolution and dispatch enforcement. It does not clamp model invocation parameters such as temperature, top_p, logprobs, output limits, or provider safety profiles. At the last trusted AI gateway or model router, derive the effective route after all caller aliases, gateway defaults, route headers, retries, provider translations, and fallback selection, then deny dispatch unless the resolved provider, provider account, model, deployment, endpoint, region, route, and fallback exactly match a verified signed route contract.",
