                "description": "<p><strong>MCP server security is a rapidly evolving production risk area.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Generic web security is not enough:</strong> secure MCP operation also requires per-request protocol metadata, routing-header/body agreement, extension negotiation, cache-scope correctness, multi-round-trip input binding, JSON Schema 2020-12 limits, and model-visible contract integrity.</li><li><strong>MCP v2 2026-07-28 is self-contained:</strong> do not recreate <code>Mcp-Session-Id</code>, sticky routing, initialize state, or a hidden global client session. Applications may use explicit opaque handles only when they are object-authorized, tenant-bound, expiring, and independently revocable.</li><li><strong>Deprecated capabilities in MCP v2 2026-07-28:</strong> enable roots, sampling, or logging only as explicitly approved deprecated-capability exceptions with method-specific budgets, telemetry, and disable controls.</li></ul>"
