                    "implementationGuidance": [
                        {
                            "id": "AID-H-037.001-G001",
                            "implementation": "Classify reasoning fields server-side, deny raw display and ordinary logging, reject client-supplied hidden state, and store only approved summaries or hashes outside break-glass.",
                            "howTo": "<h5>Concept:</h5><p>Extended-thinking systems can produce hidden reasoning blocks, summaries, signatures, or scratchpad-like metadata that should not be treated like ordinary user-visible text. The gateway should decide what can be displayed, what can be stored, what must be hashed only, and what must be round-tripped to the provider without client-side alteration.</p><h5>Step 1: Define a reasoning-trace policy</h5><pre><code class=\"language-json\">{\n  \"policy_version\": \"2026.07\",\n  \"default_display\": \"summary_only\",\n  \"raw_reasoning_display\": \"deny\",\n  \"store_raw_reasoning\": false,\n  \"store_hash\": true,\n  \"allow_client_supplied_reasoning_blocks\": false,\n  \"maximum_summary_characters\": 2000,\n  \"provider_round_trip\": {\n    \"preserve_signed_blocks_exactly\": true,\n    \"reject_modified_signed_blocks\": true\n  },\n  \"retention_days\": 30\n}\n</code></pre><h5>Step 2: Enforce display and storage controls at the AI gateway</h5><pre><code class=\"language-python\"># File: reasoning_security/trace_gate.py\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom typing import Any, Callable\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass ReasoningTraceDecision:\n    display_text: str\n    store_record: dict[str, Any]\n    blocked: bool\n    reasons: list[str]\n\n\nVerifyBreakGlass = Callable[[dict, str], bool]\nREQUIRED_POLICY = {\n    \"policy_version\", \"default_display\", \"raw_reasoning_display\",\n    \"store_raw_reasoning\", \"store_hash\", \"allow_client_supplied_reasoning_blocks\",\n    \"maximum_summary_characters\", \"provider_round_trip\", \"retention_days\",\n}\n\n\ndef sha256_text(value: str) -&gt; str:\n    return hashlib.sha256(value.encode(\"utf-8\")).hexdigest()\n\n\ndef enforce_reasoning_trace_policy(\n    response: dict[str, Any], *, policy: dict,\n    break_glass_receipt: dict | None, verify_break_glass: VerifyBreakGlass,\n) -&gt; ReasoningTraceDecision:\n    if set(policy) != REQUIRED_POLICY:\n        raise ValueError(\"verified reasoning-trace policy schema mismatch\")\n    maximum_summary = policy[\"maximum_summary_characters\"]\n    retention_days = policy[\"retention_days\"]\n    if (\n        not isinstance(maximum_summary, int) or maximum_summary &lt; 0\n        or not isinstance(retention_days, int) or retention_days &lt; 0\n    ):\n        raise ValueError(\"verified reasoning-trace policy bounds are invalid\")\n    response_id = str(response[\"id\"])\n    raw_trace = str(response.get(\"reasoning_trace\") or \"\")\n    summary = str(response.get(\"reasoning_summary\") or \"\")\n    grant_valid = (\n        break_glass_receipt is not None\n        and verify_break_glass(break_glass_receipt, response_id)\n    )\n    reasons: list[str] = []\n    if raw_trace and not grant_valid:\n        reasons.append(\"raw_reasoning_trace_hidden\")\n    display_raw = (\n        raw_trace\n        and grant_valid\n        and policy[\"raw_reasoning_display\"] == \"break_glass_only\"\n    )\n    display_text = raw_trace if display_raw else (\n        summary[:maximum_summary] if summary else \"Reasoning summary not available.\"\n    )\n    store_record: dict[str, Any] = {\n        \"response_id\": response_id,\n        \"policy_version\": policy[\"policy_version\"],\n        \"reasoning_trace_sha256\": (\n            sha256_text(raw_trace) if raw_trace and policy[\"store_hash\"] else None\n        ),\n        \"reasoning_summary\": summary[:maximum_summary] if summary else \"\",\n        \"retention_days\": retention_days,\n        \"break_glass_receipt_id\": (\n            str(break_glass_receipt[\"receipt_id\"]) if grant_valid else None\n        ),\n    }\n    if raw_trace and grant_valid and policy[\"store_raw_reasoning\"]:\n        store_record[\"raw_reasoning\"] = raw_trace\n    return ReasoningTraceDecision(display_text, store_record, False, reasons)\n\n\ndef reject_client_reasoning_state(\n    request_body: dict[str, Any], *, forbidden_fields: set[str]\n) -&gt; None:\n    supplied = sorted(key for key in request_body if key in forbidden_fields)\n    if supplied:\n        raise PermissionError(\n            \"client_supplied_reasoning_state_rejected:\" + \",\".join(supplied)\n        )</code></pre><h5>Operational verification</h5><p>Reconcile every eligible response, projection, storage, log, and analytics event. Test aliases, nested fields, client injection, serialization changes, break-glass expiry, sink failure, policy expiry, and provider-schema drift. A separately credentialed verifier reads back gateway, storage, and telemetry state; missing coverage is not PASS.</p>"
                        }
                    ]
